==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|is}} {{term|annarr|lang=non}} from the {{proto|Germanic|anþeraz|lang=is}}; whence also English {{term|other|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈanːar/|lang=is}}
*: {{rhymes|anːar|lang=is}}

===Pronoun===
{{head|is|pronoun|feminine|önnur|neuter|annað}}

# [[other]], [[another]], [[else]]

====Inflection====
Follows a regular strong adjectival declension, except for masculine accusative ''annan'' instead of *''aðran'', neuter ''annað'' instead of *''annart'' and exhibiting the Old Norse sound change ''-nnr-'' > ''-ðr-''.
{{is-decl-adj-annar}}

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|eins og hver annar}}

===Adjective (number)===
{{is-adj-01|önnur|annað}}

# {{ordinal|lang=is}} [[second]]

====Inflection====
As the pronoun (see above).

